Bugfix: Do not hang on non-regular exclusion tagfiles in the `backup` command

When a directory contained an exclusion tagfile that was not a regular
file, for example a FIFO named `CACHEDIR.TAG` with `--exclude-caches`,
restic blocked forever while opening the tagfile and could not be
interrupted. Restic now skips tagfiles that are not regular files,
prints a warning, and backs up the directory instead.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22182
